# Probes this compiler gets wrong today, one per line:
# <probe> R13-0#NN P0|P1|P2 <one-line symptom>
#
# The reason carries the R13-0 item number and its priority, so the release
# gates can be grepped out (`grep P0 tests/difftest.knownfail`).  This list is
# a ledger of known defects, not a place to hide one: a probe listed here that
# starts PASSING is a FAILURE -- closing a gap means deleting its line, so the
# list cannot rot.  Same rule as tests/c99.knownfail.
#
# Opened 2026-09-30 from the external trial of 0.0.12 (all six reproduced by
# dsh on the gate candidate df8cc9b4, the unsigned sibling of the shipped
# fb607af5).  Report: ~/unisacc-feedback-0.0.12.md.
#
# NOT listed here, deliberately -- they pass on this suite's compiler:
#   fb12-03, fb12-04, fb12-05.  difftest drives `python3 -m unisa`, the
#   reference implementation, and the reference already handles all three
#   (03 exits 0, 04 exits 22, 05 exits 8).  The defects are in the C product:
#   0.0.12 answers `undefined function 'printf'`, `not covered: width` and
#   `expected ';'`.  Listing them here would make difftest report them ok and
#   then revoke them as "listed but passing", which is a false green in both
#   directions.  They belong in a gate that runs the product; see the report
#   to cc-unisacc, 2026-09-30.
#
# R13-0b -- the subset of the real-world batch that the REFERENCE route also
# gets wrong.  Most of that batch is a product-only gap (the reference answers
# 09/10/12/13/14/15/15b/16/17/17b/18/21/23/29 exactly as cc does, while the
# product refuses or, for 18 and 23, exits 0 with wrong output) -- those live
# only in difftest.com.knownfail.  The lines below are the ones measured wrong
# on this route too, so they belong in both files.
fb12-07-missing-header-diag R13-0b#07 P1 a missing bundled header raises a location-less ValueError instead of a positioned diagnostic
fb12-08b-ulong-max-in-if R13-0b#08b P2 ULONG_MAX in an #if evaluates as 2^32, not the type's value
fb12-14-parenthesized-declarator R13-0b#14 P1 parenthesized declarator is rejected
fb12-21-indirect-call-six-args R13-0b#21 P1 indirect call with six arguments is rejected (register allocation)
fb12-31-unused-static-refs-undefined R13-0b#31 P1 unused static references are reported as undefined functions
